      "lean_source": "PaperILean/PaperIIVOutputBand.lean",
      "source_sha256": "49eb9e22685b0e49bd24b2144f31be02c16d23866ec11eb50e35c2fda28e3fb5",
      "scope": "Replacing the ordinary cubic graph row by the actual null rate preserves corresponding fibers and their common bound, multiplies the inverse density by 2|B|, and bounds the actual band output's Lebesgue length by 2(C₀−c₀)ν.",
      "hypotheses": "On a selected regular open branch, the differentiable coefficient atlas retains distinct mixed and ordinary cubic graph rows, and B has a positive uniform lower and finite upper absolute bound. The local graph is C³, the slope is differentiable and zero at the normalized endpoint, and it obeys the actual null equation. The original first-jet vanishings are unnecessary for this calculation.",
      "route": "Differentiate the actual null identity and use its cubic-row relation to construct mutually inverse output changes wherever B is nonzero. Compute the signed determinant by a row operation. Bound the projected band by two signed intervals.",
