      "scope": "The original row annihilates BA+T_z, evaluates to Δ on D, and has the exact compact model denominator (8/3)aB² with a uniform nearby lower bound. The actual moving quartic satisfies the complete body identity, the rate ratio, and its simplification along the null slice.",
      "hypotheses": "An actual quartic coefficient phase, selected smooth critical graph, actual differentiable null characteristic and its selected root identity. For the nearby estimate the compact model coefficients a and B have two-sided absolute bounds and the normalized quartic is sufficiently close in its complete coefficients. The null-slice conclusion assumes that slice along the characteristic.",
